WEBVTT

00:01:57.823 --> 00:02:00.400
We choose to go to the moon.

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:05.670
(Applause)

00:02:05.670 --> 00:02:08.584
We choose to go to the moon in this decade,

00:02:08.584 --> 00:02:10.231
and do the other things,

00:02:10.231 --> 00:02:14.560
not because they are easy, but because they are hard.

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:16.730
Jason Pontin: To contemporaries,

00:02:16.730 --> 00:02:19.983
Apollo wasn't only a victory of West over East

00:02:19.983 --> 00:02:21.198
in the Cold War.

00:02:21.198 --> 00:02:23.203
At the time, the strongest emotion

00:02:23.203 --> 00:02:24.928
was of wonder

00:02:24.928 --> 00:02:28.527
at the transcendent powers of technology.

00:02:28.527 --> 00:02:33.946
They went because it was a big thing to do.